                'Image file size (bits) = resolution × colour depth; sound file size (bits) = sample rate × resolution × length in seconds',
                'Compression reduces file size so files need less storage, less bandwidth and transmit faster',
                'Lossy compression permanently removes data (e.g. reducing resolution/colour depth, removing sounds humans cannot hear) — used for JPEG, MP3',
