              workedExample:`Question (6 marks): Explain why surgeons earn more than supermarket cashiers.

Model answer:
Supply of surgeons is low because training takes over ten years and requires high qualifications, while many people can work as cashiers after short training – so the supply curve for cashiers lies far to the right. Demand for surgeons is high because their output (saved lives, operations) is extremely valuable. With low supply and high demand, the equilibrium wage for surgeons is high; with plentiful supply, the cashier wage settles much lower.`,
