                'The crust is made of tectonic plates that move on the mantle, driven by convection currents.',
                'Divergent boundaries (plates move apart: mid-ocean ridges); convergent (plates collide: trenches, volcanoes); transform (plates slide past: earthquakes).',
                'Present-day continents formed from the break-up of supercontinents (e.g. Pangaea) over hundreds of millions of years.',
                'Tsunamis form when an undersea earthquake suddenly displaces a large volume of water; they damage coral reefs, mangroves and coastal communities.',
