                'Melting floating sea ice does not raise sea level (it already displaces its own mass of water); melting land ice does.',
                'Sea water is a mixture: water is the solvent and dissolved salts (mainly sodium chloride, also magnesium sulfate and calcium carbonate) are solutes.',
                'Salinity is measured in parts per thousand (ppt); the ocean average is about 35 ppt. The Baltic Sea is low (river input, low evaporation), the Red Sea high (high evaporation, little rain/river input).',
