                'With depth: light decreases (measured with a Secchi disc), pressure increases (about 1 atmosphere every 10 m), temperature falls, dissolved oxygen generally decreases.',
                'Upwelling: winds move surface water away so cold, nutrient-rich deep water rises, supporting high productivity.',
